      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "ENA 2643.12 recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>\"such just laws and statutes as [are contained in] this Torah</li>\n<li>which I have set before you this day\" (Deut 4:8).</li>\n<li>I was saddened by what I heard and grieved by what I saw.</li>\n<li>[margin: I was compelled by zeal to defend God and his holy name that had been profaned by Gentiles, and I said:]</li>\n<li>The scholars (<i>\u02bfulam\u0101\u02be</i>) and learned men (<i>fuqah\u0101\u02be</i>) of every nation</li>\n<li>profess statements and concepts that the common people do not understand,</li>\n<li>how much more so the concepts of men learned in the heavenly teachings</li>\n<li>and those of scholars versed in the prophetic books, as well as of those who transmit the</li>\n<li>rational and revealed laws and the traditions of the righteous prophets</li>\n<li>with unquestionable proofs and clear-cut signs.</li>\n<li>The Scriptures have attested to these things, and a multitude of</li>\n<li>intellects have confirmed them, with the result that men of understanding prescribed</li>\n<li>t[h]at these things constitute divine wisdom, there being nothing else beside them, as</li>\n<li>was confirmed by his [God's] unambiguous and truthful book in those</li>\n<li>previously mentioned verses, as well as by others found</li>\n<li>in the Scriptures. Therefore,</li>\n<li>in order for the most illustrious vizier, the crown of the vizierate, and his scholars (<i>\u02bfulam\u0101\u02be</i>) to do what is just,</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
